  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: Xを{嫉|ねた}む.\n\nUSAGE:\n{嫉|ねた}む carries a distinctly negative connotation — it implies bitter, resentful jealousy rather than innocent admiration. It is stronger and more personal than {羨|うらや}ましい (envious in a lighter sense).\n\nWRITING:\nAlso written as {妬|ねた}む. Both {嫉|ねた}む and {妬|ねた}む are used, with {妬|ねた}む being slightly more common in everyday writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {才能|さいのう}を{嫉|ねた}む: to be jealous of someone's talent\n- {成功|せいこう}を{嫉|ねた}む: to resent someone's success\n- {幸|しあわ}せを{嫉|ねた}む: to envy someone's happiness\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n{嫉妬|しっと}する is the する-verb form meaning \"to feel jealousy\" and is used more broadly in both spoken and written Japanese.",
